<header><div class="wrap">
<div class="eyebrow">Minnesota agriculture supply chain · Decision support</div>
<h1>Should UNFI adjust delivery schedules during severe winter weather?</h1>
<p>Explore 2025 weather observations near Minneapolis–Saint Paul. Use snowfall, temperature and snow depth as signals for when delivery plans may need added flexibility.</p>
</div></header>
<main>
<section class="panel">
<h2>Explore the weather observations</h2>
<p class="sub">Choose a month and measure. Adjust the snowfall threshold to see how often daily snowfall reaches your selected level.</p>
<div class="controls">
<div class="control"><label for="month">MONTH</label><select id="month"><option value="all">All of 2025</option><option value="1">January</option><option value="2">February</option><option value="3">March</option><option value="4">April</option><option value="5">May</option><option value="6">June</option><option value="7">July</option><option value="8">August</option><option value="9">September</option><option value="10">October</option><option value="11">November</option><option value="12">December</option></select></div>
<div class="control"><label for="metric">DAILY CHART MEASURE</label><select id="metric"><option value="snowfall_in">Snowfall (inches)</option><option value="avg_temp_f">Average temperature (°F)</option><option value="max_snow_depth_ft">Maximum snow depth (feet)</option><option value="freezing_hours">Hours at or below 32°F</option></select></div>
<div class="control"><label for="threshold">SNOWFALL THRESHOLD FOR FLAGGING DAYS</label><div class="sliderline"><input id="threshold" type="range" min="0.25" max="3" step="0.25" value="1"><output id="thresholdValue">1.00 in</output></div></div>
</div>
<div class="kpis">
<div class="kpi"><div class="num" id="kpiSnow">—</div><div class="lbl">Total snowfall · selected period</div></div>
<div class="kpi"><div class="num" id="kpiTemp">—</div><div class="lbl">Average temperature</div></div>
<div class="kpi"><div class="num" id="kpiFreeze">—</div><div class="lbl">Hours at/below freezing</div></div>
<div class="kpi"><div class="num" id="kpiRisk">—</div><div class="lbl">Days meeting snowfall threshold</div></div>
</div>
<div class="chartgrid" style="margin-top:24px">
<div class="chartbox"><p class="charttitle">Daily trend</p><p class="chartdesc" id="dailyCaption">Each point represents one calendar day.</p><div class="canvaswrap"><canvas id="dailyChart" role="img" aria-label="Daily weather trend chart"></canvas></div><div class="legend"><span><i class="dot"></i>Daily measure</span><span>Orange markers = snowfall at or above selected threshold</span></div></div>
<div class="chartbox"><p class="charttitle">Monthly snowfall</p><p class="chartdesc">Total daily snowfall by month across 2025.</p><div class="canvaswrap"><canvas id="monthlyChart" role="img" aria-label="Monthly snowfall bar chart"></canvas></div><div class="legend"><span><i class="dot" style="background:var(--teal)"></i>Snowfall total (inches)</span></div></div>
</div>
<p class="note">Chart values are drawn from the daily summary CSV included with this project. Hover or tap a chart point/bar for its value.</p>
</section>
<section class="panel">
<h2>Decision takeaway</h2>
<div class="insight"><strong>Recommended approach: use weather-triggered delivery flexibility, not a blanket winter schedule change.</strong>
<p>The observations show meaningful seasonal variation, including 10.517 inches of snowfall in December and 2,327 hours at or below freezing across 2025. This supports monitoring weather conditions and considering targeted adjustments when forecasts indicate disruptive conditions. It does not demonstrate that a schedule change would lower UNFI's transportation costs.</p></div>
<div class="grid2" style="margin-top:16px">
<div class="callout"><h3>When conditions look disruptive</h3><p>Review route forecasts before dispatch, communicate with carriers and receiving sites, and consider flexible arrival windows or rescheduling when snowfall and freezing conditions create operational risk.</p></div>
<div class="callout"><h3>How to test whether it saves money</h3><p>Compare on-time delivery, miles, fuel, carrier wait time, rescheduling expense, labor, inventory and spoilage before and after a pilot. Use actual UNFI shipment and cost records to measure the trade-off.</p></div>
</div>
<p class="note"><strong>Important limitation:</strong> This dataset contains weather observations for one point near Minneapolis–Saint Paul. It has no shipment records, road conditions, carrier rates, fuel costs, delivery delays, county identifiers or crop volumes. It is a weather-risk indicator, not a transportation-cost model or road-safety forecast.</p>
<div class="source"><strong>Source and coverage:</strong> Open-Meteo Historical Weather API is identified as the source in the uploaded dashboard. Location metadata: 44.956062° N, 93.20929° W; elevation 261 m; America/Chicago; January 1–December 31, 2025. The uploaded file contained daily summaries embedded in HTML; the original hourly CSV was not included. <a href="https://open-meteo.com/en/docs/historical-weather-api" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open-Meteo Historical Weather API documentation</a>.</div>
</section>
</main>
